 "title": "Base Substitution Analysis and Metabolite Extraction in Culture Samples",
 "summary": "This cluster involves the analysis of base substitutions in culture samples using various methods and tools. Genome-Wide Base Substitution Analysis is associated with several base substitution types, including C > A, C > G, C > T, T > A, T > C, and T > G. These analyses are also linked to High DO and Low DO methods. Metabolite Extraction produces Supernatant, and RNA is extracted from culture samples and sequenced using Invitrogen. The USA, Waltham, and Thermo Fisher Scientific are involved in the process, with Thermo Fisher Scientific used by Invitrogen and Waltham. The cluster also includes chemical entities such as Liquid nitrogen, NanoDrop, and culture, which are stored at culture.",
